  "notes": "Latin-inflected pop with trap-lite low end. The backbeat class is straight, but the entry is explicit that the accent grammar is not: \"backbeat on 2&4 straight but the accent grammar is a habanera/tresillo (3+3+2) rather than a plain backbeat\", so `kick.tresilloBias` is 0.66 — the highest in this section — with `secondaryAnchor` on 2a, and `hihat.base` carries the literal `tresillo` value alongside 16ths. \"The pattern deliberately omits beat 1 of some bars\" is `kick.beatSkipProb` 0.34, and \"congas/timbales colour rather than drive\" is a conga/timbale/snap perc list at a low gain. \"Trap-derived hat rolls\" keeps the roll vocabulary alive at a moderate frequency. The harmony is fully documented and is transcribed as degrees: the flagship \"is G minor alternating i—VI—V7 (Gm—E♭—D7) with i—VI(maj7)—V7\", so the families are [\"i\",\"VI\",\"V\"] with the sevenths in `extensions` and a raised `borrowed` V because a major V in a minor key is exactly what the source names. The 808 is authored because the entry names it — \"808 sub plus programmed piano-bass doubling; the bass plays the tresillo rather than the kick\" — as `counter_riff`, with `lockTo808` left low precisely because the bass does *not* follow the kick, and the bassline runs `independent_riff` on tresillo-shaped cells. Melody register is the documented G3—D5, \"a 12th written low with a nasal, forward placement\", and \"short syncopated cells in a narrow range, back-phrased against the tresillo\" is the small `motifPitchCount` and the `riff_loop`. The counter is the 2-bar montuno piano riff the entry names as the hook instrument. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because the research says \"BPM is lane-derived\"; every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the perc gain and `session.keys` beyond its first value are INFERRED — the entry names only \"the flagship is G minor\", so A minor, C minor and D minor are inferred neighbouring minor tonics and appear nowhere in the research. `bpm.mode` 105 is the midpoint of the stated 100—110 flagship band.",
